-<a id="MermaidFigures"></a>
-
-### Figures: Mermaid diagrams in documents
-
-`MermaidFigures` · `src/documents.ts:57`
-
-A figure (the layers of the graph, the tree of an impact, a timeline) is written in the Markdown document as a Mermaid diagram, in a "mermaid" block: GitHub, GitLab and most editors draw it, and it stays text, which a review compares line by line. The value says how Trame draws its figures: the reading direction of each shape, the stroke of each edge, the look of a node that is history or not in force, the Gantt chart. The colours of the statuses come from the palette.
-
-| Case | Value |
-|---|---|
-| idPrefix | n |
-| directions | { layers : down, tree : down, path : right } |
-| strokes | { computed : dottedOpen, inferred : dotted, winner : thick, support : thick, other : solid } |
-| defaultStatus | neutral |
-| history | { dashes : 4 3 } |
-| inactive | { opacity : 0.5 } |
-| gantt | { dateFormat : YYYY-MM-DD, axisFormat : %d.%m, title : Around, period : In force, today : Date of the graph, milestones : deadline, review } |
-
-- Decided by : trame
-- Rejected : Images (SVG, PNG), to regenerate at every change, and silent in a text review ; Graphviz (DOT), neither GitHub nor GitLab draws it ; PlantUML, needs a rendering server
-- Utilisé par : [Figure rendering](rendering.md#Diagrams)
-
-<a id="TextRendering"></a>
-
-### Text rendering of documents: Markdown
-
-`TextRendering` · `src/documents.ts:39`
-
-Trame's documents are written in Markdown: CommonMark, with GFM tables. They read as they are in a terminal or an editor, compare line by line in a review, and forges (GitHub, GitLab) as well as most editors display them formatted. HTML serves only for anchors and collapsible blocks. It is Trame's text rendering, hence the extension of the documents in the layout; the page is its HTML rendering, the terminal its plain-text rendering.
-
-| Case | Value |
-|---|---|
-| titleLevel | 1 |
-| sectionLevel | 2 |
-
-- Decided by : trame
-- Rejected : HTML only, unreadable as plain text, and a review no longer compares lines ; AsciiDoc or reStructuredText, less well displayed by forges and editors ; Plain text, no links, no tables, no figures
-- Utilisé par : [Markdown rendering](rendering.md#Markdown)
